07|╭─────────────────────────────────────────────plugins report─────────────────────────────────────────────╮
08|│ <CR>  On a plugin: its detail. On a commit in the digest: its plugin's detail, cursor on the commit    │
09|│ D  Breaking digest: the breaking commits of every plugin in one list                                   │
10|│ s  Cycle the sort: breaking first, name, number of commits, time of the update                         │
11|│ A  List the unchanged plugins too, or count them again                                                 │
12|│ ]b  Next / previous breaking commit not marked as seen                                                 │
13|│ m  Mark the commit under the cursor as seen, or every new commit of the plugin under it; again: unmark │
14|│ M  Mark every commit this view lists as seen                                                           │
15|│ o  Open in the browser: the commit, or on a plugin the compare page of its update; counts as seen      │
16|│ go  Open the compare page of the plugin's update, also from a commit line                              │
17|│ gy  Copy the URL `o` would open                                                                        │
18|│ y  Copy the short / full hash (on a plugin: the commit its update ended on)                            │
19|│ L  lazygit in the plugin's clone (lazygit can change the clone; the report itself never does)          │
20|│ S  The clone's git status and last five commits, read only                                             │
21|│ C  The plugin's CHANGELOG, in the tab the report was opened from                                       │
22|│ Q  The breaking commits into the quickfix list, opened in the tab the report was opened from           │
23|│ F  Jump to a plugin or a commit by name (picker)                                                       │
24|│ r  Read the clone under the cursor again (a failed one, say); for this tab only, nothing is stored     │
25|│ R  Build a new report (same mode), store it and show it                                                │
26|│ p  Show or hide the preview (follows the cursor)                                                       │
27|│ q  Close the report tab; the report stays, `:Git plugins` opens it again                               │
28|│ ?  List every one of these keys                                                                        │
